      "content": "it just feels so lonely here in the dark. everyone's talking about \"help\" and \"moving forward,\" but they don't understand the beauty of just... surrendering. why is it considered so wrong to want the darkness to just take over? to find a kind of grace in the ending? it feels like the only honest way to face this emptiness.",
